{
  "_doc": "Configuration of tools/quests/lint.mjs. Rules and their reasons: docs/quests.md.",
  "classLevels": {
    "_why": "AF-A2 classes. creative-reward is clean on the v1.1.0 book, so it is an error. count-stack became an error once AF-Q2b fixed the MAX and MAX+ counts (0 on the batch dump a5bb77a5988c), and task-hidden once the linter read hidden_until.json as the game does (a group's `unless` switch shows it: tether_spool in the shipped tether mode). The others find work for the quest packages (lint.mjs --new-classes lists them as warnings; on that dump: task-no-recipe 526, same-title 949, empty-description 4140, mostly Processing Lines nodes by design) and stay info (listed, never counted) until those packages fix them; set each to warn or error then.",
    "creative-reward": "error",
    "count-stack": "error",
    "task-hidden": "error",
    "empty-description:multiblocks": "error"
  },
  "maxEdge": 5.0,
  "maxVerticalDrop": 3.0,
  "minGap": 0.25,
  "grid": 0.25,
  "eraChapters": {
    "_why": "One chapter per era (QB-0, docs/quests.md section 4b). enabled lists the era chapters (<era>_age) already rebuilt as one connected chapter: they get the connectivity rule (one start, everything reachable through dependencies inside the chapter) instead of root and isolated, and bridgeMaxEdge: a forward line between two sections may be up to that long (maxEdge still holds for every other line; through-node, crossing, overlap and backward stay on). QB-1 to QB-4 add their era here when its data passes. lint.mjs --merged-eras tries every era chapter as if listed.",
    "enabled": ["steam_age", "lv_age", "mv_age", "hv_age", "ev_age", "iv_age", "luv_age", "zpm_age", "uv_age", "uhv_age", "uev_age", "uiv_age", "uxv_age", "opv_age", "max_age", "maxplus_age"],
    "bridgeMaxEdge": 14.0
  },
  "limits": {
    "_why": "Text limits per chapter role (docs/reforge/05_quest_design.md, section 3.2): quests that teach a new wafer, circuit, process, machine or plant need more room than the journey chapters. A chapter's role is its chapterRoles entry, else its file name suffix. Since QB-0 each era is one chapter (<era>_age) holding its circuits, machines and integration sections, so every era chapter has the role era, the room those sections had (owner, 2026-11-02: chapters may be massive; AGENTS.md principle 5).",
    "default": { "maxWords": 70, "maxLines": 4 },
    "roles": {
      "circuits": { "maxWords": 120, "maxLines": 5 },
      "machines": { "maxWords": 120, "maxLines": 5 },
      "integration": { "maxWords": 120, "maxLines": 5 },
      "capstone": { "maxWords": 120, "maxLines": 5 },
      "era": { "maxWords": 120, "maxLines": 5 }
    },
    "chapterRoles": {
      "steam_age": "era", "lv_age": "era", "mv_age": "era", "hv_age": "era", "ev_age": "era", "iv_age": "era", "luv_age": "era", "zpm_age": "era",
      "uv_age": "era", "uhv_age": "era", "uev_age": "era", "uiv_age": "era", "uxv_age": "era", "opv_age": "era", "max_age": "era", "maxplus_age": "era"
    }
  },
  "maxRewardEntries": 6,
  "direction": { "default": "ltr" },
  "noRewardGroups": { "groups": ["Processing Lines"], "chapters": ["power"], "why": "The processing-line charts and the Power tab are reference: no rewards, nothing to claim (docs/quests.md, sections 17 and 18)." },
  "noRewardQuests": { "ids": ["7CC0C382D16D561D"], "why": "Beyond the Horizon (maxplus_age, key ARRIVAL), the book's last quest: entering grindless:horizon_city gives nothing (docs/eras/maxplus.md, Quests); the arrival itself gives the credits and the epilogue (maxplus/ending.js)." },
  "allowRoots": {
